        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brass four; their hooks ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " silver, and the overlaying of their capitals and their fillets ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " silver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all the pins of the tabernacle, and of the court round about, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This is the sum of the tabernacle, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the tabernacle of testimony, as it was counted, according to the commandment of Moses, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the service of the Levites, by the hand of Ithamar, son to Aaron the priest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made all that the LORD commanded Moses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And with him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Aholiab, son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan, an engraver, and a skillful workman, and an embroiderer in blue, and in purple, and in scarlet, and fine linen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the gold that was occupied for the work in all the work of the holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", even the gold of the offering, was twenty and nine talents, and seven hundred and thirty shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the silver of them that were numbered of the congregation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hundred talents, and a thousand seven hundred and seventy five shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A bekah for every man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", half a shekel, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for every one that went to be numbered, from twenty years old and upward, for six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of the hundred talents of silver were cast the sockets of the sanctuary, and the sockets of the vail; a hundred sockets of the hundred talents, a talent for a socket.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of the thousand seven hundred seventy and five ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he made hooks for the pillars, and overlaid their capitals, and filleted them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the brass of the offering ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seventy talents, and two thousand and four hundred shekels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And with this he made the sockets to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and the brazen altar, and the brazen grate for it, and all the vessels of the altar,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.38.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.38.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the sockets of the court round about, and the sockets of the court gate, and all the pins of the tabernacle, and all the pins of the court round about.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
